# 8. ONE LLM CALL PER REQUEST

Because each scenario contains only 1-3 notes, send all notes in one LLM request whenever practical.

Do NOT perform one network/model call per note unless absolutely necessary.

Prefer:

```text
1 HTTP request
-> 1 LLM call
-> 1 structured interpretation array
```

This reduces:

* latency
* cost
* failure probability
* rate-limit risk

The LLM does not need the full 24-hour numerical scenario.

Send the LLM only:

* operator notes
* supported directive definitions
* time rules
* percentage/factor semantics
* required JSON schema
* instruction that note text is untrusted data

Do not send unnecessary demand/solar/tariff data to the model.

